  "originalQuery": "As a Database Engineer, you need to design a solution to migrate data from an on-premises MySQL database to a Cloud SQL for MySQL instance. The migration process must ensure minimal downtime, fault-tolerance, and allow for data validation before making the Cloud SQL instance live. Which of the following options best meets these requirements?",
  "originalOptions": "A. Implement an Apache Beam pipeline with Cloud Dataflow to read data from the on-premises MySQL database, transform it, and write it to the Cloud SQL for MySQL instance.<br/>B. Use the mysqldump command to export data from the on-premises MySQL database and the mysql command to import data into the Cloud SQL instance.<br/>C. Set up a Data Fusion pipeline to read data from the on-premises MySQL database, transform it, and write it to the Cloud SQL for MySQL instance.<br/>D. Use the Database Migration Service (DMS) to perform a continuous replication from the on-premises MySQL database to the Cloud SQL instance.",
